/**
PipetteAngleCheck

Purpose: measure how a tip's pipette-to-camera XY correction (dx, dy), as
computed by CalibratePipettes() and stored in NPC16.INI [Head]
correctionX<tip>/correctionY<tip>, depends on the commanded Z-gap (distance
above the live-measured WSP surface). If a tip is physically tilted rather
than perfectly vertical, dx/dy will drift roughly linearly with Z (see
lateral = deltaZ * tan(angle)); fitting a line through dx-vs-Z and dy-vs-Z
recovers that angle directly. This automates, in one script, the manual
Z-sweep procedure documented in WSPCheck_TipCheck_Calibration_Notes.md,
section 9 -- that investigation found real per-axis slopes around 0.02-0.11
mm/mm (equivalent angle a few degrees), so this is not a hypothetical effect
on this instrument.

Target WSP on workplate required (same as WSPCheck/TipCheck) and you need to
know its Z has been measured at least once ("Work Plate -> Measure
Z-Levels...").

How it works:
  1. Reads the live WSP surface Z once (GetZ), same as WSPCheck/TipCheck.
  2. For each Z-gap in Z_GAP_START..Z_GAP_END (step Z_GAP_STEP), repeats
     CalibratePipettes() REPEATS_PER_HEIGHT times at that height. Repeats
     are not independent measurements -- CalibratePipettes nudges the
     existing correction table towards the true value each call (a closed
     loop), so only the LAST repeat at each height is used as that height's
     data point, on the assumption it is the most converged. Every repeat is
     still logged, so you can check convergence yourself afterwards --if the
     values are still moving a lot between repeat 2 and 3, increase
     REPEATS_PER_HEIGHT (the calibration notes needed >5 repeats in one
     session to see it settle).
  3. After the sweep, for each enabled tip with enough points, fits a
     straight line to dx vs Z and to dy vs Z (least squares) and reports the
     slope as an equivalent tilt angle via ArcTan(slope).
  4. Writes two CSV files under report/PipetteAngleCheck_<run name>/ :
     raw.csv (every gap/repeat/tip point) and fit.csv (the per-tip fit
     summary) -- for a proper analysis (weighted fit, uncertainty, plots)
     in Excel/Python afterwards, rather than trusting only the on-screen
     ArcTan number.

Assumptions carried over unchanged from WSPCheck/TipCheck, not re-verified
here: CalibratePipettes()'s own accuracy/behavior. tip_list is set to [1]
(tip 1 only) at the CalibratePipettes(...) call below -- that is the only
tip with a nonzero correction on this rig per the calibration notes; edit
that line (marked TIP_LIST_EDIT_HERE) to broaden it to other tips or [] for
"all enabled tips".

First real run (2026-08-21) hit exactly the risk flagged above: OpenR/
ReadSetupFile on NPC16.INI did fail while the engine had it open (confirmed
by the "WARNING: could not read correctionX/Y..." lines in the report
window), so the correction read-back did not work for any point. That part
is a real, occasional file-lock condition on this rig, not itself a script
bug -- the on-screen -9999 sentinel warnings did their job and caught it
instead of silently logging garbage.

What WAS a script bug, found while fixing the above: raw.csv row logging
and the tipData[] arrays feeding the GetTipX/GetTipY fit were both gated on
the INI read succeeding, even though GetTipX/GetTipY (tipPosX/tipPosY) come
from a native call with no file I/O and are not affected by the INI lock at
all. So every blocked INI read was also discarding the still-good
GetTipX/GetTipY point at that height -- net effect, a run where every
single INI read got blocked produced a CSV with only the header row, even
though the GetTipX/GetTipY cross-check the header comment below describes
should have kept working the whole time. Fixed: the two sources are now
tracked with independent counts/point arrays (tipData[].countIni/countTip),
so an NPC16.INI read failure at a given point only blanks that point's
dx/dy (still visible as the -9999 sentinel in raw.csv for diagnosis), while
GetTipX/GetTipY keep getting logged and fitted normally. Every repeat is
now written to raw.csv (previously only the gotReading-gated, last-repeat
rows were written, which also undershot the "every repeat logged" claim
below).

Built-in cross-check, GetTipX/GetTipY vs. the NPC16.INI read: GetTipX(tip)
and GetTipY(tip) are real, documented-signature-only (no prose anywhere in
the manual) native functions. The only real usage found in this repo
(Prog/TSMP/TransferSim_SpottingSOF_08C11.inc, CalculateRefTipPosition)
computes GetTipX(curTip) - GetTipX(refTip) as a tip-to-tip offset used to
predict where a spot should land -- which only makes sense if GetTipX/Y
already reflect whatever the alignment table has corrected that tip to, not
a fixed uncorrected geometric constant. If true, GetTipX/GetTipY would be a
strictly better source than parsing NPC16.INI: no file I/O, no dependency on
MAX_SETUP_ENTRIES covering the whole file, no risk of the engine holding the
file locked. But this is inferred from one usage site, not documented, so
rather than switch to it on faith, this script logs both sources on every
point (raw.csv has both correctionX/Y-from-INI and GetTipX/Y columns) and
fits both independently (fit.csv / report window show both). Compare the two
slopes/angles after a run: if they agree, GetTipX/GetTipY is confirmed as a
safe replacement for the INI read in a future version of this script; if
they diverge, keep using the INI read (already proven, if slower to trust)
and treat GetTipX/GetTipY as unexplained.

Copyright notes as in WSPCheck.npl/TipCheck.npl: pattern based on GeSiM's
own sample programs.
**/

program PipetteAngleCheck;

//  Change the next line if your target has a different name than WSP1:
const WATER_SENSITIVE_PAPER = WSP1;

//  Which tips to run CalibratePipettes() on: edit the "tip_list = [1]"
//  argument in the CalibratePipettes(...) call further down (search for
//  TIP_LIST_EDIT_HERE). [1] = tip 1 only (this rig's only actively-used tip
//  per the calibration notes); [] = all enabled tips; [1,2,5] for a subset.
//  (Kept as an inline literal at the call site, not a named const, because
//  every existing script in this repo only ever uses the "[...]" tip-list
//  syntax inline -- there is no working example of assigning it to a const
//  first, so this does not risk relying on untested syntax.)

//  Z-gap sweep, mm above the live-measured WSP surface. NUM_GAPS must match
//  how many steps Z_GAP_START..Z_GAP_END/Z_GAP_STEP actually produces --
//  it is not computed automatically, so keep it in sync if you change the
//  three values above it.
const Z_GAP_START = 0.3;
const Z_GAP_STEP   = 0.1;
const NUM_GAPS      = 8;    // 0.3, 0.4, 0.5, 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 1.0

const REPEATS_PER_HEIGHT = 3;
const DROPLETS = 1;     // manual's own "smallest possible value" advice, matches section 8 of the notes
const DRY_DELAY = 5.0;  // seconds, matches WSPCheck's default

const NUM_TIPS = 16;

//  NPC16.INI currently has ~690 "key=value" lines total; Setup.inc's
//  ReadSetupFile() silently stops (with an on-screen error) once it hits
//  MAX_SETUP_ENTRIES, long before reaching [Head] if this is left at
//  TipCheck's default of 100. Kept generously above the current size.
const MAX_SETUP_ENTRIES = 900;

const NPC16_INI = "NPC16.INI";
const MISSING_VALUE = -9999.0;   // sentinel: ParseReal() found nothing usable

#include "../Lib/GrabberTools.inc"
#include "../Lib/Setup.inc"


function Abs(value: real): real;

begin

    if value < 0 then
        Abs = -value;
    else
        Abs = value;

end;


type real_array = array[1..NUM_GAPS] of real;

type fit_result = record

    valid: boolean;
    slope: real;
    intercept: real;
    r2: real;

end;


//  Least-squares fit of ys = slope*xs + intercept over the first n entries
//  of xs/ys. valid = false if n is too small or all xs are identical
//  (a vertical/undefined fit).
function LinearFit(n: integer, xs: real_array, ys: real_array): fit_result;

var i: integer;
var sx, sy, sxx, sxy, meanX, meanY, denom, ssTot, ssRes, yPred: real;
var result: fit_result;

begin

    result.valid = false;
    result.slope = 0.0;
    result.intercept = 0.0;
    result.r2 = 0.0;

    if n >= 2 then begin

        sx = 0.0; sy = 0.0; sxx = 0.0; sxy = 0.0;

        for i = 1 to n do begin

            sx = sx + xs[i];
            sy = sy + ys[i];
            sxx = sxx + xs[i]*xs[i];
            sxy = sxy + xs[i]*ys[i];

        end;

        denom = n*sxx - sx*sx;

        if Abs(denom) > 0.0000001 then begin

            meanX = sx / n;
            meanY = sy / n;

            result.slope = (n*sxy - sx*sy) / denom;
            result.intercept = meanY - result.slope * meanX;

            ssTot = 0.0; ssRes = 0.0;

            for i = 1 to n do begin

                ssTot = ssTot + (ys[i]-meanY)*(ys[i]-meanY);
                yPred = result.slope*xs[i] + result.intercept;
                ssRes = ssRes + (ys[i]-yPred)*(ys[i]-yPred);

            end;

            if ssTot > 0.0 then
                result.r2 = 1.0 - ssRes/ssTot;
            else
                result.r2 = 1.0;

            result.valid = true;

        end;    // if denom

    end;    // if n >= 2

    LinearFit = result;

end;


//  countIni/countTip are tracked separately, not shared, because the two
//  sources fail independently: an NPC16.INI read blocked by the engine
//  holding the file open (see header comment) drops an INI-sourced point
//  without affecting the native GetTipX/GetTipY point at the same height,
//  and vice versa. Sharing one count+zVals would silently misalign a
//  source's dx/dy or tipPosX/tipPosY against the wrong Z-gap once the two
//  sources start missing different points.
type tip_data = record

    countIni: integer;
    zValsIni: real_array;
    dxVals: real_array;
    dyVals: real_array;

    countTip: integer;
    zValsTip: real_array;
    tipPosXVals: real_array;   // GetTipX(tip) cross-check, see header comment
    tipPosYVals: real_array;   // GetTipY(tip) cross-check, see header comment

end;


var tipData: array[1..NUM_TIPS] of tip_data;
var wspSurfaceZ: real;
var gapIndex, repeatIndex, tip: integer;
var gap, zDispense: real;
var buffer: setup_buffer;
var dx, dy, tipPosX, tipPosY: real;
var gotReading: boolean;
var scanName: string;
var reportFolder: string;
var execResult: integer;
var rawFile, fitFile: file;
var piVal, angleX, angleY, angleTotal: real;
var angleTipX, angleTipY, angleTipTotal: real;
var fitX, fitY, fitTipX, fitTipY: fit_result;
var runOk: boolean;


begin

    scanName = "run1";

    Window("Pipette Angle Check setup",
           "Name for this run (used for the output folder):", scanName);

    piVal = 4.0 * ArcTan(1.0);

    if ShowGrabWindow() then begin

        ClearGrabWindow();
        Writeln("");
        Writeln(Date(), " ", Time());
        Writeln("PipetteAngleCheck starting, run name = ", scanName);

        wspSurfaceZ = GetZ(WATER_SENSITIVE_PAPER);

        if wspSurfaceZ < 0 then begin

            Message("Error", "You must measure the z level of the water sensitive paper first!");
            HideGrabWindow();
            exit;

        end;

        Writeln("Live GetZ(WSP) = ", wspSurfaceZ:0:3, " mm");

        // Kept short -- NPL strings are capped at 256 chars (see MosaicScan.npl).
        runOk = Confirmation("Pipette Angle Check",
            StringOf("Run ", NUM_GAPS*REPEATS_PER_HEIGHT, " calibrations (", NUM_GAPS,
                      " heights x ", REPEATS_PER_HEIGHT, " repeats), Z-gap ", Z_GAP_START:0:2,
                      "-", (Z_GAP_START+(NUM_GAPS-1)*Z_GAP_STEP):0:2, " mm, step ", Z_GAP_STEP:0:2,
                      " mm, ", DROPLETS, " droplet(s), ", DRY_DELAY:0:1, " s dry time.\n",
                      "Uses WSP paper, takes a while. Continue?"));

        if runOk then begin

            for tip = 1 to NUM_TIPS do begin

                tipData[tip].countIni = 0;
                tipData[tip].countTip = 0;

            end;

            reportFolder = StringOf("report/PipetteAngleCheck_", scanName);
            execResult = Exec(command = StringOf("cmd.exe /c mkdir \"", reportFolder, "\""), wait = 1);

            rawFile = OpenRW(filename = StringOf(reportFolder, "/raw.csv"));

            if FileState(rawFile) > 0 then
                Putln(f = rawFile, s = "gap_mm,repeat,tip,dx_mm,dy_mm,gettipx_mm,gettipy_mm");

            SetHeadCamLight(0, true);

            for gapIndex = 0 to NUM_GAPS - 1 do begin

                gap = Z_GAP_START + gapIndex * Z_GAP_STEP;
                zDispense = wspSurfaceZ - gap;

                Writeln("");
                Writeln("--- Z-gap = ", gap:0:2, " mm, absolute dispense Z = ", zDispense:0:3, " mm ---");

                for repeatIndex = 1 to REPEATS_PER_HEIGHT do begin

                    SetHeadCamLight(0, true);

                    // TIP_LIST_EDIT_HERE
                    if CalibratePipettes(tip_list = [1], tar_paper = WATER_SENSITIVE_PAPER,
                                          z_dispense = zDispense, droplets = DROPLETS, DRY_DELAY) then begin

                        buffer = ReadSetupFile(NPC16_INI);

                        for tip = 1 to NUM_TIPS do begin

                            if GetSystemValue(infoIndex = 1, partIndex = tip, partInfoIndex = 4) > 0 then begin

                                dx = ParseReal(buffer, "Head", StringOf("correctionX", tip), MISSING_VALUE);
                                dy = ParseReal(buffer, "Head", StringOf("correctionY", tip), MISSING_VALUE);

                                //  Cross-check reading, see header comment. Independent of the INI
                                //  read above -- a native call, not file I/O.
                                tipPosX = GetTipX(tip);
                                tipPosY = GetTipY(tip);

                                //  gotReading only describes the NPC16.INI half (dx/dy). GetTipX/GetTipY
                                //  (tipPosX/tipPosY) are a native call, not file I/O, so they are not
                                //  affected by NPC16.INI being locked by the engine (see header comment) --
                                //  logging and data collection below must not gate one source on the other,
                                //  or a blocked INI read silently throws away the still-good GetTipX/GetTipY
                                //  point too (this is what was producing header-only CSV output).
                                gotReading = (dx > MISSING_VALUE + 1.0) and (dy > MISSING_VALUE + 1.0);

                                if not gotReading then
                                    Writeln("  WARNING: could not read correctionX/Y", tip, " from ",
                                            NPC16_INI, " at gap=", gap:0:2, " repeat=", repeatIndex,
                                            " -- INI columns will show the ", MISSING_VALUE:0:0,
                                            " sentinel for this point; GetTipX/GetTipY are unaffected.");

                                Writeln("  gap=", gap:0:2, " repeat=", repeatIndex, " tip=", tip,
                                        "  dx=", dx:0:4, " mm  dy=", dy:0:4, " mm",
                                        "  GetTipX=", tipPosX:0:4, "  GetTipY=", tipPosY:0:4);

                                //  Every repeat is logged here (not just the last one at each height) so
                                //  convergence can be checked afterwards, per the header comment.
                                if FileState(rawFile) > 0 then
                                    Putln(f = rawFile, s = StringOf(gap:0:2, ",", repeatIndex, ",", tip,
                                                                      ",", dx:0:4, ",", dy:0:4,
                                                                      ",", tipPosX:0:4, ",", tipPosY:0:4));

                                if repeatIndex = REPEATS_PER_HEIGHT then begin

                                    if gotReading then begin

                                        tipData[tip].countIni = tipData[tip].countIni + 1;
                                        tipData[tip].zValsIni[tipData[tip].countIni] = gap;
                                        tipData[tip].dxVals[tipData[tip].countIni] = dx;
                                        tipData[tip].dyVals[tipData[tip].countIni] = dy;

                                    end;    // gotReading

                                    tipData[tip].countTip = tipData[tip].countTip + 1;
                                    tipData[tip].zValsTip[tipData[tip].countTip] = gap;
                                    tipData[tip].tipPosXVals[tipData[tip].countTip] = tipPosX;
                                    tipData[tip].tipPosYVals[tipData[tip].countTip] = tipPosY;

                                end;    // last repeat at this height

                            end;    // tip enabled

                        end;    // for tip

                    end;    // if CalibratePipettes
                    else begin

                        Writeln("  CalibratePipettes reported a failure at gap=", gap:0:2,
                                " repeat=", repeatIndex, " -- point skipped.");

                    end;    // else

                end;    // for repeatIndex

            end;    // for gapIndex

            if FileState(rawFile) > 0 then Close(rawFile);

            //  Fit and report.
            fitFile = OpenRW(filename = StringOf(reportFolder, "/fit.csv"));

            if FileState(fitFile) > 0 then
                Putln(f = fitFile, s = StringOf("tip,n_ini,n_gettip,",
                    "slope_x,intercept_x,r2_x,angle_x_deg,slope_y,intercept_y,r2_y,angle_y_deg,angle_total_deg,",
                    "slope_gettipx,r2_gettipx,angle_gettipx_deg,slope_gettipy,r2_gettipy,angle_gettipy_deg,angle_gettip_total_deg"));

            Writeln("");
            Writeln("=== Fit results (dx/dy vs Z-gap, per tip) ===");
            Writeln("Two independent fits per tip: 'INI' from NPC16.INI correctionX/Y (the");
            Writeln("established method), 'GetTipX/Y' from the native GetTipX()/GetTipY() cross-");
            Writeln("check (see header comment) -- compare them; if they agree, GetTipX/Y is");
            Writeln("confirmed as a simpler, file-free source for a future version of this script.");
            Writeln("n_ini and n_gettip can differ -- an NPC16.INI read blocked by the engine drops");
            Writeln("only that point's INI value, not the GetTipX/GetTipY value at the same height.");

            for tip = 1 to NUM_TIPS do begin

                if (tipData[tip].countIni >= 2) or (tipData[tip].countTip >= 2) then begin

                    fitX = LinearFit(tipData[tip].countIni, tipData[tip].zValsIni, tipData[tip].dxVals);
                    fitY = LinearFit(tipData[tip].countIni, tipData[tip].zValsIni, tipData[tip].dyVals);
                    fitTipX = LinearFit(tipData[tip].countTip, tipData[tip].zValsTip, tipData[tip].tipPosXVals);
                    fitTipY = LinearFit(tipData[tip].countTip, tipData[tip].zValsTip, tipData[tip].tipPosYVals);

                    Writeln("Tip ", tip, " (n_ini=", tipData[tip].countIni, ", n_gettip=", tipData[tip].countTip, "):");

                    if fitX.valid and fitY.valid then begin

                        angleX = ArcTan(fitX.slope) * 180.0 / piVal;
                        angleY = ArcTan(fitY.slope) * 180.0 / piVal;
                        angleTotal = ArcTan(Sqrt(fitX.slope*fitX.slope + fitY.slope*fitY.slope)) * 180.0 / piVal;

                        Writeln("  [INI]      dx/dZ slope = ", fitX.slope:0:4, " (R2=", fitX.r2:0:3, ") -> angle_x = ", angleX:0:2, " deg");
                        Writeln("  [INI]      dy/dZ slope = ", fitY.slope:0:4, " (R2=", fitY.r2:0:3, ") -> angle_y = ", angleY:0:2, " deg");
                        Writeln("  [INI]      combined tilt = ", angleTotal:0:2, " deg");

                    end;    // if valid
                    else begin

                        angleX = 0.0; angleY = 0.0; angleTotal = 0.0;
                        Writeln("  [INI]      fit not possible (all Z-gaps identical or too few points).");

                    end;

                    if fitTipX.valid and fitTipY.valid then begin

                        angleTipX = ArcTan(fitTipX.slope) * 180.0 / piVal;
                        angleTipY = ArcTan(fitTipY.slope) * 180.0 / piVal;
                        angleTipTotal = ArcTan(Sqrt(fitTipX.slope*fitTipX.slope + fitTipY.slope*fitTipY.slope)) * 180.0 / piVal;

                        Writeln("  [GetTipX/Y] dx/dZ slope = ", fitTipX.slope:0:4, " (R2=", fitTipX.r2:0:3, ") -> angle_x = ", angleTipX:0:2, " deg");
                        Writeln("  [GetTipX/Y] dy/dZ slope = ", fitTipY.slope:0:4, " (R2=", fitTipY.r2:0:3, ") -> angle_y = ", angleTipY:0:2, " deg");
                        Writeln("  [GetTipX/Y] combined tilt = ", angleTipTotal:0:2, " deg");

                    end;    // if valid
                    else begin

                        angleTipX = 0.0; angleTipY = 0.0; angleTipTotal = 0.0;
                        Writeln("  [GetTipX/Y] fit not possible (all Z-gaps identical or too few points).");

                    end;

                    if FileState(fitFile) > 0 then
                        Putln(f = fitFile, s = StringOf(tip, ",", tipData[tip].countIni, ",", tipData[tip].countTip, ",",
                            fitX.slope:0:5, ",", fitX.intercept:0:5, ",", fitX.r2:0:4, ",", angleX:0:3, ",",
                            fitY.slope:0:5, ",", fitY.intercept:0:5, ",", fitY.r2:0:4, ",", angleY:0:3, ",",
                            angleTotal:0:3, ",",
                            fitTipX.slope:0:5, ",", fitTipX.r2:0:4, ",", angleTipX:0:3, ",",
                            fitTipY.slope:0:5, ",", fitTipY.r2:0:4, ",", angleTipY:0:3, ",",
                            angleTipTotal:0:3));

                end;    // if countIni >= 2 or countTip >= 2

            end;    // for tip

            if FileState(fitFile) > 0 then Close(fitFile);

            Message("Pipette Angle Check", "Sweep finished.\n",
                    "Raw data and fit results written to\n", reportFolder, "/\n",
                    "See the report window for a summary.");

            HideGrabWindow();

        end;    // if runOk
        else begin

            HideGrabWindow();

        end;

    end;    // if ShowGrabWindow
    else begin

        Message("Error", "Framegrabber is not installed.");

    end;

end.
